title: skgconfig.toml
pid: 1cc77936-d29e-4f82-81d4-fb59ffb83fda
body: |2-
  The server's configuration file. See example-data/ for an example.

  Pass its path as a command-line argument (default: =data/jeff/skgconfig.toml=) when starting the server (see =bash/start-servers.sh=). The directory containing the file is the *data root*; all relative paths in the config are resolved against it. A relative path may leave the data root: a config in =data/jeff/= names a skgrepo in =data/claude/public= as =../claude/public=, and its =..= is resolved when the config loads.
